Q: Flutter Web - No Firebase App &#39;[DEFAULT]&#39; has been created - call Firebase App.initializeApp() (app/no-app) A: <p>For anyone checking this in 2026, with Flutter, Firebase Web and mobile support, the issue is that web requires no name parameter and mobile does in some cases so the solution is just simply this:</p>
<pre><code>    await Firebase.initializeApp(
      name: kIsWeb ? null : 'appName',
      options: DefaultFirebaseOptions.currentPlatform,
    );
</code></pre>
